PDFium — AGG23 rasterizer port shape, CMYK-to-sRGB table, and shading/blend-mode formulas

PlumePDF's Phase 8 raster core (`src/PlumePdf/Raster/Agg/ScanlineRasterizer.cs`,
`OutlineRasterizer.cs`, `CurveFlattener.cs`, `StrokeGenerator.cs`) is a field-by-field clean-room
port of PDFium's vendored AGG 2.3 (`third_party/agg23/agg_rasterizer_scanline_aa.h`,
`agg_rasterizer_cells_aa.h`, `agg_curves.h`, `agg_vcgen_stroke.h`) — AGG 2.3 specifically, since
2.5+ relicensed under the GPL and is off-limits under the clean-room policy. `src/PlumePdf/Raster/Color/DeviceCmyk.cs`'s
9×9×9×9 CMYK→sRGB lookup table is likewise a field-by-field port of PDFium's
`core/fxge/dib/cfx_cmyk_to_srgb.cpp`, and `Raster/Shading/AxialShading.cs`/`RadialShading.cs`
follow the projection formula in PDFium's `core/fpdfapi/render/cpdf_rendershading.cpp`. Per the clean-room policy (AGENTS.md), every one of these is a reimplementation from the algorithm's
published shape and behavior against PlumePDF's own types — PDFium's source was read and its
algorithm structure followed, not copied; see the provenance comment at the top of each port's
